.sh 1 "ABSTRACT"
.pp
SMAL Hero is a symbolic macro assembly language for the Heathkit Hero-1
robot.  The assembler accepts the standard mnemonics for the Motorola
6800 instruction set, as well as a set of special extended mnemonics for
the Hero-1 Robot Control Language interpreter.  In addition to providing
the basic assembly functions the SMAL Hero assembler provides a powerful
macro facility and a linkage editor facility supporting separate assembly,
subprogram libraries, and shared common blocks.  Assembler and linker
output may be either absolute or relocatable, and the object language is
encoded in an easily interpreted textual form.
.pp
The SMAL Hero assembler is a variant of the Machine Independent SMAL
assembler,
originally developed at the University of Iowa as a tool for teaching
and research.
Assemblers in the SMAL family are
written in highly machine independent Pascal, and have been successfully
transported between a number of Pascal implementations.
.bp
